diff --git a/research/integration/stream_readiness_b8n5_v1/SOURCES.md b/research/integration/stream_readiness_b8n5_v1/SOURCES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..741b175
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research/integration/stream_readiness_b8n5_v1/SOURCES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Source and literature record
+
+Repository intake pinned at4c701cc51b06296268ad8d9ae3eff1dd6f2d379d, GitHub MCP.
+Read README(blob7aa60f1c2e151724b0696a54b75267e62faa1787), active CURRENT_GOAL
+(blobcb65e252e30b3552e960b1ee335ca6229be09d14), ROADMAP
+(blob6c79de4666772d7bf3230a182d20631be6ff2d0b), recent open/closed Issues,
+open PRs, first100 branch names and targeted readiness/receipt/BufferedReader
+searches. GitHub Issues#4362/#4359/#4355/#4369/#4367 and PRs#4381/#4377/#4375/
+#4354/#4351 observed; all are excluded. Closed#3876 read; its no-authority,
+ordered notification requirements motivate this integration constraint but its
+original allocation is not repeated. Query visibility is bounded/non-atomic.
+
+Just-in-time receipt branch search found#4390's owner for the previous r9k4
+publication. This worker does not duplicate that delivery. Exact r9k4 ZIP537817
+bytes SHA256d26d4c840ecbf6bbfae7d3da0968425066c6e92a97f7e5d7cdf034882cfc95b0
+was read-only restored; unchanged verifier checked971 manifest members and18
+frozen files, reproduced old audit/controls/development results and pure units.
+New old-study actor runs0. Result receipt is in provenance/R9K4_REAUDIT.json.
+Original ZIP is separately retained in the conversation; not nested here.
+
+Primary background accessed2026-09-26 (online3.13.15 docs; actual build separately
+recorded, not assumed the same patch version):
+- https://docs.python.org/3.13/library/io.html — BufferedReader may read ahead
+  and return buffered data on subsequent reads; readline waits for LF or EOF.
+- https://docs.python.org/3.13/library/select.html — readiness is on descriptors;
+  a Python file object contributes its fileno, not its complete-message buffer.
+- https://docs.python.org/3.13/library/os.html#os.read — raw byte read contract.
+- https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/pipe.7.html — pipes are byte streams;
+  nonblocking empty state versus EOF; no message boundaries.
+
+The experiment tests the documented composition on the supplied build; it does
+not claim a new I/O algorithm. No source from an operation-specific blocked
+GitHub publication is imported or resent.
diff --git a/research/integration/stream_readiness_b8n5_v1/TOOL_SURFACE_NOTE.md b/research/integration/stream_readiness_b8n5_v1/TOOL_SURFACE_NOTE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a0e8ac5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research/integration/stream_readiness_b8n5_v1/TOOL_SURFACE_NOTE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# Tool-surface diagnostic preserved
+
+After pilot batch0, the interactive tool display appended a terminal-clear escape
+and `TERM environment variable not set.`. Inspection immediately afterward found
+pilot_receipts/batch-0.stderr and execution/pilot/batch-0/stderr both exactly
+zero bytes, outer shell status0, all16 first cases complete, unchanged raw auditor
+PASS with818 checks. The text was not in the retained experimental subprocess
+streams, so it is not attributed to either scientific actor. No missing receipt
+was inferred and no case was retried. Later container calls used a non-login shell.
+This changed only the outer shell invocation, not any frozen source, process argv,
+clock contract or experimental decision. The original tool display cannot be
+reconstructed from zero-byte subprocess logs; this note preserves that limitation.
